Subject: WTF: Phoenix threads: stack bounds, 1 MiB default stacks, pointer pthread_key_t, no ucontext yet

StackBounds come from pthread_getattr_np() on the calling thread (a local compat until libphoenix
has it, track B1). The libphoenix default thread stack is 256 KiB, so WTF asks for 1 MiB as it does
for musl. pthread_key_t is a pointer on Phoenix, so the invalid key is nullptr. There is no
ucontext_t until SA_SIGINFO delivery lands (track B4), so PlatformRegisters is the stack pointer
only (no HAVE(MACHINE_CONTEXT)).

